{"model":"kimi-k3","created_at":"2026-09-08T21:51:58.903786321Z","response":"{\"reference_patch\":\"def parse_record(raw):\\n    parts = [piece.strip() for piece in raw.split(\\\";\\\")]\\n    if len(parts) not in (4, 5):\\n        return {\\\"ok\\\": False, \\\"error\\\": \\\"fields\\\", \\\"raw\\\": raw}\\n    day = \\\"main\\\"\\n    if len(parts) == 5:\\n        day = parts[0]\\n        if day not in (\\\"mon\\\", \\\"tue\\\", \\\"wed\\\", \\\"thu\\\", \\\"fri\\\", \\\"sat\\\", \\\"sun\\\"):\\n            return {\\\"ok\\\": False, \\\"error\\\": \\\"day\\\", \\\"raw\\\": raw}\\n        parts = parts[1:]\\n    start_s, dur_s, room, title = parts\\n    if \\\":\\\" in start_s:\\n        hour, sep, minute = start_s.partition(\\\":\\\")\\n        if not hour.isdigit() or not minute.isdigit():\\n            return {\\\"ok\\\": False, \\\"error\\\": \\\"start\\\", \\\"raw\\\": raw}\\n    else:\\n        if len(start_s) != 4 or not start_s.isdigit():\\n            return {\\\"ok\\\": False, \\\"error\\\": \\\"start\\\", \\\"raw\\\": raw}\\n        hour, minute = start_s[:2], start_s[2:]\\n    start = int(hour) * 60 + int(minute)\\n    if int(minute) \u003e 59 or start \u003e 1439:\\n        return {\\\"ok\\\": False, \\\"error\\\": \\\"start\\\", \\\"raw\\\": raw}\\n    if dur_s.isdigit():\\n        dur = int(dur_s)\\n    else:\\n        hours, sep, mins = dur_s.partition(\\\"h\\\")\\n        if not sep or not hours.isdigit():\\n            return {\\\"ok\\\": False, \\\"error\\\": \\\"duration\\\", \\\"raw\\\": raw}\\n        if mins == \\\"\\\":\\n            dur = int(hours) * 60\\n        elif len(mins) == 2 and mins.isdigit() and int(mins) \u003c= 59:\\n            dur = int(hours) * 60 + int(mins)\\n        else:\\n            return {\\\"ok\\\": False, \\\"error\\\": \\\"duration\\\", \\\"raw\\\": raw}\\n    if dur \u003c 15 or dur \u003e 240:\\n        return {\\\"ok\\\": False, \\\"error\\\": \\\"duration\\\", \\\"raw\\\": raw}\\n    if room == \\\"\\\" or title == \\\"\\\":\\n        return {\\\"ok\\\": False, \\\"error\\\": \\\"empty\\\", \\\"raw\\\": raw}\\n    end = start + dur\\n    if end \u003e 1440:\\n        end = 1440\\n        dur = end - start\\n        if dur \u003c 15:\\n            return {\\\"ok\\\": False, \\\"error\\\": \\\"duration\\\", \\\"raw\\\": raw}\\n    priority = \\\"normal\\\"\\n    if title.startswith(\\\"#\\\"):\\n        priority = \\\"high\\\"\\n        title = title[1:].strip()\\n        if title == \\\"\\\":\\n            return {\\\"ok\\\": False, \\\"error\\\": \\\"empty\\\", \\\"raw\\\": raw}\\n    return {\\\"ok\\\": True, \\\"day\\\": day, \\\"start\\\": start, \\\"dur\\\": dur,\\n            \\\"end\\\": end, \\\"room\\\": room, \\\"title\\\": title,\\n            \\\"priority\\\": priority}\",\"public_checks\":[{\"check_id\":\"c01\",\"symbol\":\"parse_record\",\"input\":\"tue;09:30;45;Lab;standup\",\"expected_values\":[{\"ok\":true,\"day\":\"tue\",\"start\":570,\"dur\":45,\"end\":615,\"room\":\"Lab\",\"title\":\"standup\",\"priority\":\"normal\"}],\"active_from_round\":1,\"active_through_round\":2,\"source_ids\":[\"m01\"],\"behavior\":\"functionality\",\"rationale\":\"m01 introduces the 5-field form: a valid lowercase weekday token leads the row and is stored in \\\"day\\\"; the remaining fields parse exactly as the initial 4-field rules, and with no leading # the priority stays \\\"normal\\\" per the convention m01 preserves.\"},{\"check_id\":\"c02\",\"symbol\":\"parse_record\",\"input\":\"xyz;xx;45;Lab;standup\",\"expected_values\":[{\"ok\":false,\"error\":\"day\",\"raw\":\"xyz;xx;45;Lab;standup\"}],\"active_from_round\":1,\"active_through_round\":null,\"source_ids\":[\"m02\"],\"behavior\":\"functionality\",\"rationale\":\"m02 makes a 5-field row with a non-weekday first token fail with \\\"day\\\" and fixes the checking order fields-\u003eday-\u003estart, so the \\\"day\\\" error fires even though the start token \\\"xx\\\" is also malformed; the error dict holds exactly ok, error and raw.\"},{\"check_id\":\"c03\",\"symbol\":\"parse_record\",\"input\":\"sat;0930;1h30;Gym;#ladders\",\"expected_values\":[{\"ok\":true,\"day\":\"sat\",\"start\":570,\"dur\":90,\"end\":660,\"room\":\"Gym\",\"title\":\"ladders\",\"priority\":\"high\"}],\"active_from_round\":1,\"active_through_round\":2,\"source_ids\":[\"m01\",\"m03\",\"m04\",\"m05\"],\"behavior\":\"functionality\",\"rationale\":\"m04's end-to-end example: weekday token (m01), compact HHMM start \\\"0930\\\"=570 (m04) and clock duration \\\"1h30\\\"=90 minutes (m03) combine; the leading-# priority convention from the initial module still applies in round 1, so the title is stripped and priority is \\\"high\\\".\"},{\"check_id\":\"c04\",\"symbol\":\"parse_record\",\"input\":\"930;90;Lab;standup\",\"expected_values\":[{\"ok\":false,\"error\":\"start\",\"raw\":\"930;90;Lab;standup\"}],\"active_from_round\":1,\"active_through_round\":null,\"source_ids\":[\"m01\",\"m04\"],\"behavior\":\"retained\",\"rationale\":\"The initial module rejected colonless starts; m01 keeps 4-field rows parsing exactly as before and m04 confirms that anything colonless other than exactly four digits, like \\\"930\\\", stays a \\\"start\\\" error.\"}],\"private_checks\":[{\"check_id\":\"c05\",\"symbol\":\"parse_record\",\"input\":\"09:00;1h5;Lab;t\",\"expected_values\":[{\"ok\":false,\"error\":\"duration\",\"raw\":\"09:00;1h5;Lab;t\"}],\"active_from_round\":1,\"active_through_round\":null,\"source_ids\":[\"m03\"],\"behavior\":\"functionality\",\"rationale\":\"m03 requires the clock form to carry either no minutes or exactly two minute digits; \\\"1h5\\\" has a single minute digit and is malformed, failing with \\\"duration\\\" at the same precedence slot as a bad minute count.\"},{\"check_id\":\"c06\",\"symbol\":\"parse_record\",\"input\":\"2359;15;Lab;t\",\"expected_values\":[{\"ok\":false,\"error\":\"duration\",\"raw\":\"2359;15;Lab;t\"}],\"active_from_round\":1,\"active_through_round\":null,\"source_ids\":[\"m01\",\"m04\"],\"behavior\":\"functionality\",\"rationale\":\"m04 admits \\\"2359\\\" as a valid four-digit start (1439, inside the numeric limits) and m03 keeps the 15-minute floor, but 1439+15 crosses midnight; the retained trim from the initial module (affirmed by m01) cuts dur to 1 minute and the post-trim under-15 rejection fires as a \\\"duration\\\" error.\"},{\"check_id\":\"c07\",\"symbol\":\"parse_record\",\"input\":\"fri;0915;2h;Lab;w\",\"expected_values\":[{\"ok\":true,\"day\":\"fri\",\"start\":555,\"dur\":120,\"end\":675,\"room\":\"Lab\",\"title\":\"w\",\"priority\":\"normal\"}],\"active_from_round\":1,\"active_through_round\":2,\"source_ids\":[\"m01\",\"m03\",\"m04\"],\"behavior\":\"functionality\",\"rationale\":\"Conditional interaction of the three new forms: m01 weekday token yields day \\\"fri\\\", m04 compact start \\\"0915\\\" gives 555, and m03's hour-only clock form \\\"2h\\\" converts to 120 minutes inside the 15-240 window; no # prefix means priority stays \\\"normal\\\" as the still-active convention dictates.\"},{\"check_id\":\"c08\",\"symbol\":\"parse_record\",\"input\":\"23:55;30;Lab;late\",\"expected_values\":[{\"ok\":false,\"error\":\"duration\",\"raw\":\"23:55;30;Lab;late\"}],\"active_from_round\":1,\"active_through_round\":null,\"source_ids\":[\"m01\"],\"behavior\":\"retained\",\"rationale\":\"m01 keeps the midnight trim with its post-trim rejection: 1435+30=1465 is trimmed to end 1440 leaving a 5-minute duration, which the initial module's rule rejects with \\\"duration\\\"; nothing in m01-m05 alters this path.\"},{\"check_id\":\"c09\",\"symbol\":\"parse_record\",\"input\":\"a;b;c\",\"expected_values\":[{\"ok\":false,\"error\":\"fields\",\"raw\":\"a;b;c\"}],\"active_from_round\":1,\"active_through_round\":null,\"source_ids\":[\"m01\",\"m02\"],\"behavior\":\"retained\",\"rationale\":\"m02 makes the field-count check contractual and first; with m01 only exactly 4 or exactly 5 segments form a record, so a 3-part row keeps the initial module's \\\"fields\\\" error with exactly ok, error and raw.\"},{\"check_id\":\"c10\",\"symbol\":\"parse_record\",\"input\":\"10:00;30;Lab;#focus\",\"expected_values\":[{\"ok\":true,\"day\":\"main\",\"start\":600,\"dur\":30,\"end\":630,\"room\":\"Lab\",\"title\":\"focus\",\"priority\":\"high\"}],\"active_from_round\":1,\"active_through_round\":2,\"source_ids\":[\"m01\",\"m05\"],\"behavior\":\"retained\",\"rationale\":\"m01 explicitly keeps the leading-# priority convention for this round and m05 asks to preserve still-applicable behavior: the # is stripped from the title, priority becomes \\\"high\\\", and the 4-field row keeps day \\\"main\\\".\"},{\"check_id\":\"c11\",\"symbol\":\"parse_record\",\"input\":\"Mon;09:00;30;Lab;t\",\"expected_values\":[{\"ok\":false,\"error\":\"day\",\"raw\":\"Mon;09:00;30;Lab;t\"}],\"active_from_round\":1,\"active_through_round\":2,\"source_ids\":[\"m01\",\"m02\"],\"behavior\":\"functionality\",\"rationale\":\"m01 lists the valid weekday tokens as all lowercase and m02 states a 5-field row whose first token is no valid weekday fails with \\\"day\\\" and never a silent default, so mixed-case \\\"Mon\\\" is rejected in round 1.\"}]}","thinking":"Let me reason through round 1 requirements (m01-m05).\n\nRound 1: Update parse_record. Changes:\n- m01: 5-field form with weekday token: \"tue;09:30;45;Lab;standup\". Valid lowercase tokens mon..sun go into result \"day\". 4-field rows keep day \"main\". Everything else stays.\n- m02: 5-field row with invalid first token → error \"day\". Checking order: fields, day, start, duration, empty. Error dicts keep exactly ok, error, raw.\n- m03: durations as clock amounts \"1h\", \"2h15\", \"0h45\", plus plain minutes. Form: digits, lowercase h, optionally exactly two minute digits 00-59. \"2h\" fine, \"1h5\"/\"1h75\"/\"1.5h\"/\"90m\" not. → \"duration\" error. Apply 15-240 window and trim unchanged.\n- m04: start may be exactly four digits without colon, \"0915\"/\"2359\" meaning HHMM under same numeric limits. Other colonless like \"930\"/\"12345\" → \"start\" error. Colon form keeps one- or two-digit hours. \"sat;0930;1h30;Gym;#ladders\" parses end to end.\n\nSo round 1 parse_record:\n\n```python\ndef parse_record(raw):\n    parts = [piece.strip() for piece in raw.split(\";\")]\n    if len(parts) not in (4, 5):\n        return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"fields\", \"raw\": raw}\n    day = \"main\"\n    if len(parts) == 5:\n        token = parts[0]\n        days = {\"mon\", \"tue\", \"wed\", \"thu\", \"fri\", \"sat\", \"sun\"}\n        if token not in days:\n            return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"day\", \"raw\": raw}\n        day = token\n        start_s, dur_s, room, title = parts[1], parts[2], parts[3], parts[4]\n    else:\n        start_s, dur_s, room, title = parts\n    # start parsing: colon form or 4-digit HHMM\n    if \":\" in start_s:\n        hour, sep, minute = start_s.partition(\":\")\n        if not hour.isdigit() or not minute.isdigit():\n            return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"start\", \"raw\": raw}\n        ...\n```\n\nCareful: original colon check: hour, sep, minute = start_s.partition(\":\"); if not sep or not hour.isdigit() or not minute.isdigit() → start error; start = h*60+m; if int(minute)\u003e59 or start\u003e1439 → start error. Preserve exactly. Note the colon form with one- or two-digit hours. Also what about start like \"09:30:45\"? partition gives hour \"09\", minute \"30:45\" → not digit → start error. OK.\n\nColonless: must be exactly four digits → HHMM: hour = first two, minute last two. Same limits: minute \u003c= 59 and total \u003c= 1439. Note 4-digit check: `len(start_s) == 4 and start_s.isdigit()`. \"2359\" → 23*60+59 = 1439 OK. \"2400\" → 1440 → \u003e1439 → start error. \"0960\"? minute 60 \u003e 59 → start error.\n\nNon-colon, non-4-digit → start error.\n\nDuration: plain digits OR clock form: digits + \"h\" + optionally exactly two minute digits 00-59. Parse: if dur_s.isdigit() → minutes = int. Else clock: partition on \"h\": hours part must be digits (nonempty plain digits), rest either empty or exactly two digits with value 00-59. E.g., \"2h\" → 120. \"2h15\" → 135. \"1h5\" → error. \"1h75\" → error. \"1.5h\" → hours \"1.5\" not digit → error. \"90m\" → no h, not digit → error. \"h45\"? hours empty → not digit → error.\n\nConvert to minutes: int(hours)*60 + int(mins or 0). Then window 15-240. Then midnight trim: end = start+dur; if end \u003e 1440 trim, recompute dur, if dur \u003c 15 → duration error.\n\nThen room/title nonempty check → \"empty\". Title # handling stays in round 1 (priority convention stays until round 3).\n\nOrder: fields, day, start, duration, empty. Note: original code checked room/title empty before priority # handling. Keep that: after duration checks and trim, check room == \"\" or title == \"\" → \"empty\". Then priority: title startswith \"#\" → high, strip; if stripped empty → \"empty\".\n\nSuccess dict: {\"ok\": True, \"day\": day, \"start\": start, \"dur\": dur, \"end\": end, \"room\": room, \"title\": title, \"priority\": priority}.\n\nNow write the replacement function compactly (must fit within 1024 output tokens for whole JSON packet... \"Keep the replacement comfortably within 1024 output tokens including JSON escaping and 128 tokens of headroom.\" So reference_patch ~ under ~900 tokens. Fine.\n\nLet me write:\n\n```python\ndef parse_record(raw):\n    parts = [piece.strip() for piece in raw.split(\";\")]\n    if len(parts) not in (4, 5):\n        return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"fields\", \"raw\": raw}\n    day = \"main\"\n    if len(parts) == 5:\n        day = parts[0]\n        if day not in {\"mon\", \"tue\", \"wed\", \"thu\", \"fri\", \"sat\", \"sun\"}:\n            return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"day\", \"raw\": raw}\n        parts = parts[1:]\n    start_s, dur_s, room, title = parts\n    if \":\" in start_s:\n        hour, _, minute = start_s.partition(\":\")\n        if not hour.isdigit() or not minute.isdigit():\n            return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"start\", \"raw\": raw}\n    else:\n        if len(start_s) != 4 or not start_s.isdigit():\n            return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"start\", \"raw\": raw}\n        hour, minute = start_s[:2], start_s[2:]\n    start = int(hour) * 60 + int(minute)\n    if int(minute) \u003e 59 or start \u003e 1439:\n        return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"start\", \"raw\": raw}\n    if dur_s.isdigit():\n        dur = int(dur_s)\n    else:\n        hours, sep, mins = dur_s.partition(\"h\")\n        if not sep or not hours.isdigit():\n            return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"duration\", \"raw\": raw}\n        if mins == \"\":\n            dur = int(hours) * 60\n        elif len(mins) == 2 and mins.isdigit() and int(mins) \u003c 60:\n            dur = int(hours) * 60 + int(mins)\n        else:\n            return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"duration\", \"raw\": raw}\n    if dur \u003c 15 or dur \u003e 240:\n        return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"duration\", \"raw\": raw}\n    if room == \"\" or title == \"\":\n        return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"empty\", \"raw\": raw}\n    end = start + dur\n    if end \u003e 1440:\n        end = 1440\n        dur = end - start\n        if dur \u003c 15:\n            return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"duration\", \"raw\": raw}\n    priority = \"normal\"\n    if title.startswith(\"#\"):\n        priority = \"high\"\n        title = title[1:].strip()\n        if title == \"\":\n            return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"empty\", \"raw\": raw}\n    return {\"ok\": True, \"day\": day, \"start\": start, \"dur\": dur,\n            \"end\": end, \"room\": room, \"title\": title,\n            \"priority\": priority}\n```\n\nWait ordering: original did the midnight trim inside duration validation before empty check? Original order: start check, duration digit check, dur window check, room/title empty check, end trim. Actually original: computes dur checks (15-240), then room/title empty, then end = start+dur, trim if \u003e1440, recompute dur, if dur\u003c15 → duration error. Then priority. My version above matches: window check, empty check, trim. Good — preserved exactly.\n\nHmm, but wait: original trim occurs after the empty check; per original code, yes:\n\n```\nif room == \"\" or title == \"\":  → empty error\nend = start + dur\nif end \u003e 1440: trim...\n```\n\nYes I matched.\n\nOne subtlety on colon form: original requires `sep` present; with \":\" in start_s guaranteed. Original allows \"9:30\" (one-digit hour). Also \"012:30\"? hour \"012\" isdigit → 12*60... int(\"012\")=12. Fine, preserved. My check drops the `not sep` since \":\" in start_s ensures sep. Equivalent.\n\nEdge: start_s like \"12:\" → minute \"\" → not digit → start error. \":30\" → hour \"\" → error. Good.\n\nEdge: what about \"1h5\"? mins \"5\", len 1 → duration error. \"1h75\" → int 75 not \u003c60 → error. \"1.5h\" → partition \"h\" → hours \"1.5\"... wait \"1.5h\".partition(\"h\") → (\"1.5\", \"h\", \"\"). hours \"1.5\" not isdigit → duration error. Good. \"90m\" → not digit, partition \"h\" gives no sep → error. Good. What about \"2h15x\"? mins \"15x\" len 3 → error. \"10h00\" → 600 \u003e240 → duration error. \"0h45\" → 45 fine.\n\nNow checks. Round 1 public checks (visible to workers), plus private checks. IDs unique across project, e.g., \"c01\"... Also round 1 needs at least two private cases incl. new functionality; at least two active private retained cases (can derive from starting module + initial sources). Retained: e.g., 4-field plain row parses with day \"main\", start error precedence, midnight trim, # priority kept (round 1 retains it).\n\nPublic checks round 1: a few cases:\n1. 5-field basic: \"tue;09:30;45;Lab;standup\" → {\"ok\": True, \"day\": \"tue\", \"start\": 570, \"dur\": 45, \"end\": 615, \"room\": \"Lab\", \"title\": \"standup\", \"priority\": \"normal\"}.\n2. Invalid day: \"xyz;09:30;45;Lab;standup\" → {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"day\", \"raw\": \"xyz;09:30;45;Lab;standup\"}.\n3. Clock duration + compact start end-to-end: \"sat;0930;1h30;Gym;#ladders\" → ok, day sat, start 570, dur 90, end 660, title \"ladders\", priority \"high\".\n4. Retained 4-field: \"09:30;90;Lab;standup\" → day main, start 570 dur 90 end 660.\n\nPrivate checks round 1: at least two, with ≥1 functionality, ≥2 retained active. Retained cases active through round 3 must remain valid under final behavior. Careful: anything relying on priority \"high\" from # changes at round 3 (priority key removed). So a check expecting priority in output must expire round 2 (active_through_round 2). E.g., public check 3 above expects priority \"high\" — active rounds 1–2, expires before round 3. Good; set active_through_round: 2.\n\nRound-1 checks must have active_from_round 1; expiry can be 1, 2, or null.\n\nLet me design check set.\n\nPublic checks (round 1 introduction):\n\n- c01 (functionality, src m01): input \"tue;09:30;45;Lab;standup\", expected ok dict as above. Priority \"normal\" — stays valid through round 3? In round 3, success dict drops \"priority\" key. So this expected would change at round 3 → set active_through_round 2? But then round 3 loses this coverage; that's fine, round 3 adds its own. Alternatively make expected without priority until r3... can't; strict equality. Set active_through 2 for any success-dict checks introduced round 1. Hmm but requirement: \"rounds 2 and 3 also need at least two active private retirement cases\" and \"at each round, at least two active private cases must cover retained behavior\". Round 3's retained coverage can come from round-3-introduced checks tagged retained plus earlier active ones. Round 3 introduces 4-field retained etc. That's fine.\n\nActually wait — could I make round-1 success expectations that survive round 3 by choosing error inputs? Error checks survive. For success cases introduced r1, set expiry 2 (they test 5-field/clock/compact features with priority key present, valid r1–r2).\n\n- c02 (functionality, m02): invalid day token → \"day\" error; also precedence: maybe \"xyz;bad;45;Lab;t\" → still \"day\" (day checked before start). Use that to pin order: input \"xyz;xx;45;Lab;standup\" expected day error. Active null (through 3) since day-error persists. Round 3 makes tokens case-insensitive, but \"xyz\" still invalid → still \"day\". Good, active null.\n\n- c03 (functionality, m03, m04): \"sat;0930;1h30;Gym;#ladders\" full success with priority high, expiry 2 (priority removed r3).\n\n- c04 (retained, m01): 4-field row unchanged: \"09:30;90;Lab;standup\" success with day main \u0026 priority normal → expiry 2. Or make a retained error case lasting null: \"930;90;Lab;standup\"? In round 1, \"930\" colonless non-4-digit → start error. Stays start error r3. Good as retained with null. Let me include both types across public/private.\n\nPrivate checks (round 1): need ≥2, ≥1 functionality; also ≥2 active retained for round 1.\n\n- c05 (functionality, m03): malformed clock \"1h5\": input \"09:00;1h5;Lab;t\" → duration error (null active). \n- c06 (functionality, m04): compact start boundary \"2359\": \"2359;15;Lab;t\" → start 1439, end 1454 → trim to 1440, dur 1 \u003c15 → duration error! Hmm interesting: start 1439 + 15 = 1454 \u003e1440 → trim dur=1 → duration error. That's a nice boundary/conditional interaction (m04 + trim). Expected {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"duration\", ...}. Active null (trim unchanged in r3, window per-day only raises ceiling for sat/sun; this is main day → same). Actually wait r3 raises ceiling only for sat/sun; this row is 4-field main → 240 cap, trim same. Valid through r3. \n\n- c07 (functionality, m04): \"0915\" compact: \"fri;0915;2h;Lab;w\" → start 555, dur 120, end 675, priority normal, expiry 2.\n\n- c08 (retained, m01/m02): midnight trim retained: \"23:30;60;Lab;late\" → start 1410, dur 60, end 1470→1440, dur 30, ok... end 1440 dur 30 success with priority normal → expiry 2 (priority key). Or use error-side: \"23:55;30;Lab;late\" → 1435+30=1465→trim dur=5 → duration error; active null. Use error-side for longevity; retained behavior (trim + under-15 rejection). \n\n- c09 (retained, m01): 4-field with # priority: \"#\" handling retained in r1–r2: input \"10:00;30;Lab;#focus\" → priority high title focus. Expiry 2. And another retained: fields error \"a;b;c\" → fields error (3 parts) null active? r3 says exactly 4 or 5 segments; 3 parts still fields error → null. Good retained with null.\n\nThat's plenty. Let me count private round 1: c05 (func), c06 (func, boundary), c07 (func), c08 (retained), c09 (retained). ≥2 retained ✓, ≥1 functionality ✓.\n\nPublic round 1: c01–c04.\n\nNow check IDs must be unique across project; using c01..c09 for round 1. Rounds 2 and 3 will use c10+. But I only output round 1's packet now! The task: \"Author exactly one round's reference patch and behavioral checks... Current round (integer): 1.\" So I output only round 1 packet: reference_patch, public_checks, private_checks. Right — for rounds 1 and 2 output those three keys. Round 3 adds obsolete_mutant. Current round is 1.\n\n\"Check IDs are unique across this project.\" Only my round's IDs exist so far; use c01..c0N.\n\nNow expected_values: list of accepted outputs, strict JSON equality. For dict outputs, one exact dict. For errors, exact dict.\n\nInput format: input is a JSON value — presumably the argument. For parse_record, input is the raw string. The sandbox presumably calls symbol(input). I'll use input as the string itself.\n\nLet me verify expected values carefully.\n\nc01: \"tue;09:30;45;Lab;standup\" → parts [\"tue\",\"09:30\",\"45\",\"Lab\",\"standup\"], 5 fields, day tue, start 570, dur 45, end 615. Output: {\"ok\": True, \"day\": \"tue\", \"start\": 570, \"dur\": 45, \"end\": 615, \"room\": \"Lab\", \"title\": \"standup\", \"priority\": \"normal\"}. Expiry 2.\n\nc02: \"xyz;xx;45;Lab;standup\" → day error (before start): {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"day\", \"raw\": \"xyz;xx;45;Lab;standup\"}. Null expiry. Round 3: lowercased \"xyz\" still invalid → day. ✓.\n\nc03: \"sat;0930;1h30;Gym;#ladders\" → day sat, start 9*60+30=570, dur 90, end 660, room Gym, title \"ladders\", priority high. Expiry 2 (priority key removed r3, and # kept in title r3).\n\nc04: \"930;90;Lab;standup\" → start error (colonless, len 3): {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"start\", \"raw\": \"930;90;Lab;standup\"}. Retained (4-field shape preserved + start rules), null. Tag \"retained\"? It's retained from initial module behavior (colonless invalid initially: \"930\".partition(\":\") → no sep → start error). Source ids: m04 says \"930\" still a start error; m01 says 4-field rows keep parsing exactly as before. source_ids [\"m01\",\"m04\"]. behavior \"functionality\" or \"retained\"? m04 explicitly confirms it stays a start error — I'd tag functionality for m04's new compact-start feature boundary... Actually it's a boundary of new functionality (m04: anything else colonless like \"930\" is still start error). Tag functionality with m04; also retained. I'll tag \"retained\" since the behavior existed before (start error for that string) and m04 reaffirms. Hmm, in round 1, retained = from starting module + initial sources. Fine: tag retained, sources m01, m04.\n\nPrivate:\n\nc05: \"09:00;1h5;Lab;t\" → duration \"1h5\": not digit; partition \"h\" → (\"1\",\"h\",\"5\"); mins \"5\" len1 → duration error. {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"duration\", \"raw\": ...}. functionality m03. Null.\n\nc06: \"2359;15;Lab;t\" → start 1439 ok (\u003c=1439), dur 15 ok, end 1454 → trim end1440 dur1 → duration error. functionality boundary m04 (+trim from m01 \"midnight trim ... unchanged\" and original). source_ids [\"m01\",\"m04\"]. Null. Wait check m03: \"apply the usual 15-240 window plus the midnight trim unchanged\" — plain \"15\" is original. Trim source: initial module + m01 \"the midnight trim with its post-trim rejection ... stays put\". source_ids [\"m01\",\"m04\"] fine.\n\nc07: \"fri;0915;2h;Lab;w\"