ity\" ✓ (c05, c06, c07, c11 functionality). \"at least two active private cases must cover retained behavior\" — c08, c09, c10 tag retained ✓. Public checks count separately; private checks required — fine.\n\nBehaviors tags: c01 functionality (m01), c02 functionality (m02), c03 functionality (m01/m03/m04), c04 retained (m01/m04), c05 functionality (m03), c06 functionality (m01/m04), c07 functionality, c08 retained (m01), c09 retained (m01/m02), c10 retained (m01), c11 functionality (m01/m02 — boundary, all-lowercase rule).\n\nRationales: cite message specifics.\n\nNow write reference_patch text with escaped \\n in JSON.\n\nPatch:\n\ndef parse_record(raw):\n    parts = [piece.strip() for piece in raw.split(\";\")]\n    if len(parts) not in (4, 5):\n        return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"fields\", \"raw\": raw}\n    day = \"main\"\n    if len(parts) == 5:\n        day = parts[0]\n        if day not in (\"mon\", \"tue\", \"wed\", \"thu\", \"fri\", \"sat\", \"sun\"):\n            return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"day\", \"raw\": raw}\n        parts = parts[1:]\n    start_s, dur_s, room, title = parts\n    if \":\" in start_s:\n        hour, sep, minute = start_s.partition(\":\")\n        if not hour.isdigit() or not minute.isdigit():\n            return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"start\", \"raw\": raw}\n    else:\n        if len(start_s) != 4 or not start_s.isdigit():\n            return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"start\", \"raw\": raw}\n        hour, minute = start_s[:2], start_s[2:]\n    start = int(hour) * 60 + int(minute)\n    if int(minute) \u003e 59 or start \u003e 1439:\n        return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"start\", \"raw\": raw}\n    if dur_s.isdigit():\n        dur = int(dur_s)\n    else:\n        hours, sep, mins = dur_s.partition(\"h\")\n        if not sep or not hours.isdigit():\n            return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"duration\", \"raw\": raw}\n        if mins == \"\":\n            dur = int(hours) * 60\n        elif len(mins) == 2 and mins.isdigit() and int(mins) \u003c= 59:\n            dur = int(hours) * 60 + int(mins)\n        else:\n            return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"duration\", \"raw\": raw}\n    if dur \u003c 15 or dur \u003e 240:\n        return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"duration\", \"raw\": raw}\n    if room == \"\" or title == \"\":\n        return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"empty\", \"raw\": raw}\n    end = start + dur\n    if end \u003e 1440:\n        end = 1440\n        dur = end - start\n        if dur \u003c 15:\n            return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"duration\", \"raw\": raw}\n    priority = \"normal\"\n    if title.startswith(\"#\"):\n        priority = \"high\"\n        title = title[1:].strip()\n        if title == \"\":\n            return {\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"empty\", \"raw\": raw}\n    return {\"ok\": True, \"day\": day, \"start\": start, \"dur\": dur,\n            \"end\": end, \"room\": room, \"title\": title,\n            \"priority\": priority}\n\nCheck token count: ~450 tokens, fine.\n\nNote: unused variable `sep` in colon branch — harmless.\n\nDouble-check c06: \"2359;15;Lab;t\": 4 parts; start_s \"2359\" no colon, len4 digits → hour \"23\", minute \"59\" → start 1439, minute 59 ≤59, start ≤1439 ok. dur 15 ok. room/title nonempty. end 1454 \u003e1440 → end 1440, dur 1 → \u003c15 → duration error ✓.\n\nc08: \"23:55;30;Lab;late\": start 1435; dur 30; end 1465 → trim dur 5 → duration error ✓.\n\nc11 expiry 2: at r3, \"Mon\" lowercase→\"mon\" valid. So expected would differ at r3 → expiry 2 correct ✓.\n\nc10 expiry 2: r3 removes priority and keeps \"#focus\" verbatim ✓ expires before r3 ✓.\n\nc01 expiry 2: r3 removes priority key → expected changes ✓ expiry 2.\n\nc03 expiry 2: same ✓ (also # handling).\n\nc07 expiry 2: priority key ✓.\n\nSo public active r3: c02, c04 survive. Fine; later rounds add their own.\n\nNo conflicting same-input cases. IDs c01–c11 unique.\n\nRationales (compact):\n\nc01: m01 introduces 5-field weekday form w